{"kind":"request","text":"Head outcome recovery for a hold\n\nChild of J4 under ruling0790129e. Data and design only, placed after the J4 live witness and before J5. The first S1 scratch room retains an accepted hold whose one head attempt is recorded unknown; its fork stays creating with no seed. Existing head answers require that attempt's own answer, HOLD_ATTEMPTS.head=1, and WorkspaceHost has no head recovery/replies port. Source recovery report89922e3f records why another current ref read cannot substitute.\n\nDesign either a declared recovery read bound to the exact original provider reference and attempt, read once and recorded as that attempt's late answer with its ordinal, or an explicit retry step with its own declared attempt count. State how the journal observer records a genuine late outcome and retains unknown history. Explain authority, provenance, timing, replay, restart and no-resend limits. The bounded original-operation diagnostic proposal belongs here; it reads one authenticated journal, binds the accepted hold/head opening and ordinal, and projects fixed metadata only. No arbitrary private bodies, no provider probe and no manufactured outcome.\n\nRecord the custody limit: the original head provider helper can create and revoke a temporary READ token; unknown does not prove which stage ran or revocation/absence. Preserve original lane, hold, room and evidence unchanged. Deliver a reviewed design using current kernel filing rules; implementation needs a separate request/ruling. Do not begin before the J4 live witness.","body":{"conditions":"Data and design only, after the J4 live witness and before J5. No implementation, provider probe or retry authorization.","parent":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0c3091fa54f38d3709dcb7a741d6754c420ad10c","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0790129efe51158f9239fc92d51288166d6843d8, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:89922e